; etyme.com — DNS zone, updated 2026-11-09 to put the app on etyme.com.
; Host: Bluehost (ns1.bluehost.com, ns2.bluehost.com). Enter these in
; Bluehost → Domains → etyme.com → DNS. TTLs in seconds.
;
; Read against the live zone on 2026-11-09. Lines marked CHANGED or NEW
; differ from it; everything else is kept exactly as it is.

$ORIGIN etyme.com.
$TTL 14400

; ── Nameservers (unchanged) ────────────────────────────────────────────
@                       86400  IN  NS     ns1.bluehost.com.
@                       86400  IN  NS     ns2.bluehost.com.

; ── The app ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; CHANGED: was 216.24.57.1 (the old site, on another host). Now the
; Vercel project etyme2040. If Vercel's Domains page shows a different
; A value or CNAME for this project, use Vercel's.
@                         900  IN  A      76.76.21.21
; CHANGED: was a CNAME to etyme.com (which followed the old site).
www                       900  IN  CNAME  cname.vercel-dns.com.
; NEW: Tapin's company page (the app maps tapin.etyme.com to /site/tapin).
tapin                     900  IN  CNAME  cname.vercel-dns.com.

; REMOVED: the wildcard  *  900 IN A 216.24.57.1
; It sent every unknown name (notify, _dmarc, in, tapin, ...) to the old
; host, which is why notify.etyme.com never carried Resend's records.
; Do not point a wildcard at Vercel from Bluehost: Vercel issues a
; certificate for *.etyme.com only when its own nameservers hold the
; zone. Each firm's <slug>.etyme.com is added by name until then.

; ── Google Workspace mail for @etyme.com (unchanged) ───────────────────
@                              IN  MX 1   aspmx.l.google.com.
@                              IN  MX 5   alt1.aspmx.l.google.com.
@                              IN  MX 5   alt2.aspmx.l.google.com.
@                              IN  MX 10  alt3.aspmx.l.google.com.
@                              IN  MX 10  alt4.aspmx.l.google.com.

; CHANGED: the zone had two SPF records, which makes SPF fail for every
; message (a domain may publish only one). Merged into one, keeping every
; sender either listed.
@                              IN  TXT    "v=spf1 ip4:162.144.178.127 include:_spf.google.com include:spf.smtp.adxemailhelp.com ~all"

; Google site verification (unchanged)
@                              IN  TXT    "google-site-verification=BBDibdPX9tTYPhaDsrVgPeKBEqMiCXs8rZjrf4WbfYk"
@                              IN  TXT    "google-site-verification=cxCyQld11ghvCXM09SlUlmD1aVXzandjIVzX9EPXQlc"
@                              IN  TXT    "google-site-verification=hxgsHBmOvl9N-eZ2B67Y-NIuWG2-L0t0SZeDnTrb4z8"

; NEW: DMARC, report-only, so nothing is rejected while SPF settles.
_dmarc                         IN  TXT    "v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:support@etyme.com"

; ── Etyme's outgoing notices from notify.etyme.com, via Resend (NEW) ───
; Without these Resend cannot verify notify.etyme.com, and sign-up
; confirmations and notices do not leave. Copy the DKIM value, and the
; MX host if its region differs, exactly from Resend → Domains →
; notify.etyme.com; the placeholder below is not a real key.
send.notify                    IN  MX 10  feedback-smtp.us-east-1.amazonses.com.
send.notify                    IN  TXT    "v=spf1 include:amazonses.com ~all"
resend._domainkey.notify       IN  TXT    "p=PASTE-THE-DKIM-KEY-FROM-RESEND"

; ── Not added on purpose ───────────────────────────────────────────────
; in.etyme.com (forwarded business email) stays without records: the
; inbound door is closed until EMAIL_INTAKE_LIVE=1.
